WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:00.763
Welcome.

2
00:00:00.763 --> 00:00:04.780
This is the technical deep
dive for DNS, DHCP and IPAM,

3
00:00:04.780 --> 00:00:08.887
one of the books of the
Federal Modernization Workbook.

4
00:00:08.887 --> 00:00:13.451
It's for the network and DDI engineers
who will design the resolution paths,

5
00:00:13.451 --> 00:00:16.837
move authority off Active
Directory, and run the result.

6
00:00:16.837 --> 00:00:18.399
It comes in two parts.

7
00:00:18.399 --> 00:00:20.539
Part 1 covers the hard surfaces:

8
00:00:20.539 --> 00:00:24.735
split-brain DNS and what Active
Directory DNS really carries,

9
00:00:24.735 --> 00:00:27.532
the places queries escape agency policy,

10
00:00:27.532 --> 00:00:32.550
and the DNS identity and DNSSEC work
underneath certificates and tokens.

11
00:00:32.550 --> 00:00:36.512
Part 2 builds and runs the control
plane: cloud private endpoints,

12
00:00:36.512 --> 00:00:40.914
IPAM as the authority for address
blocks, the reference architecture,

13
00:00:40.914 --> 00:00:44.950
then the six-phase migration and
the evidence that keeps it honest.

14
00:00:44.950 --> 00:00:49.490
Vendors appear only as the book's
examples, never as endorsements.
